vi: "+ and "* are the clipboard and the primary selection

The registers + and * (as Vim's) yank into /dev/clip0 and /dev/clip0p and put what they
hold now; where those files don't exist (Linux) they are ordinary registers (BMDS: clipboard).

--- a/editors/vi.c	2026-10-07 01:05:26.497623706 -0700
+++ b/editors/vi.c	2026-10-07 01:05:26.537090802 -0700
@@ -397,8 +397,12 @@
 #if ENABLE_FEATURE_VI_YANKMARK
 	smalluint YDreg;//,Ureg;// default delete register and orig line for "U"
